  "note": "Early results, re-weighted to the final count later. NBC, ABC, AP, CBS, CNN, Fox News and MS NOW share this one SSRS poll (over 75,000 voters nationally; in person, online and by phone, plus a pre-election survey for early and mail voters), so other networks will repeat these numbers, not add a second opinion. In the vote-by-group tables the columns are NBC's Democrat and Republican columns; they match the U.S. House vote (for example 2% Democratic among those voting to support Trump), but NBC's text does not label them, and no overall House total has been published. Numbers come from NBC's national table; its live blog quotes a few subgroup figures that differ, and those are not used. Tables refreshed at 9:15 PM ET: shares move by about a point as more respondents are added; groups I could not match to NBC's current table keep their earlier numbers. Rows refreshed through NBC's 9:22 PM ET update where they could be matched safely; shares move by about a point as more respondents are added, so a few groups may lag by a point.",
